# Remote-build sync excludes for rch (honored by TransferPipeline::sync_to_remote,
# in addition to the 39 patterns in ~/.config/rch/config.toml).
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: every remote build was failing in the transfer stage with
#   sync_to_remote: timed out after 145000ms
# three internal retries per worker, before any Cargo started - ten consecutive failures
# across hz3 and hz4. The global config already drops .git/, .beads/, target/ and
# tests/artifacts/, but it does NOT drop this repo's two Python virtualenvs, and they
# dominate what is left: .venv is 444M and venv is 201M, ~60% of a ~1.1G payload that has
# to cross the wire inside a 145s budget while sibling projects contend for the same
# workers.
#
# EVERY PATTERN BELOW IS GITIGNORED, i.e. none of it is tracked source, so excluding it
# cannot remove a build input. Deliberately NOT listed: fuzz/ (holds real cargo-fuzz build
# targets a remote `cargo fuzz` would need), artifacts/ and tests/ (both tracked).
#
# Scoped to this repo on purpose. The alternative - adding these to exclude_patterns in
# ~/.config/rch/config.toml - would change sync behaviour for every project and agent on
# this host, which is not a call one repo's build should make.

# Python virtualenvs: ~645M, never usable by a remote cargo build
.venv/
venv/

# Tool caches: regenerated on demand, never a build input
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.hypothesis/
